===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sengʷʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|song}}, {{m|enm|sang}}, from {{inh|en|ang|sang}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*sangu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sangwaz|t=singing, song}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sengʷʰ-|t=to sing}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|sang}}, {{m|sco|song||singing, song}}, {{cog|stq|Song||song}}, {{cog|fy|sang||song}}, {{cog|nl|zang||song}}, {{cog|nds|sang||song}}, {{cog|de|Sang||singing, song}}, {{cog|sv|sång||song}}, {{cog|nb|sang||song}}, {{cog|nn|song||song}}, {{cog|is|söngur||song}}, {{cog|grc|ὀμφή||voice, oracle}}. More at {{l|en|sing}}.

